{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.CharZero.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.half_unit_breaks_normalizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.half_unit_breaks_normalizer","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/schwinger-measure-computational-time.lean#L95-L112","doc":"**Exact distinguisher (proved, unconditional).** A half unit breaks the\nmoment/normalizer match at every order: `c·m! ≠ m!` for any `c` satisfying\n`2·c = 1`, over any characteristic-zero commutative ring. This records, at\nthe fibre-algebra level, the exploration's `n!/2 ≠ n!` distinguisher between\nthe ρ-split reading (`ς = 1`, the ½ in the channel split) and the\nenergy-Jacobian reading (`ς = 1/2` on the proper-time side).\n\n§7c: the half is carried by its defining relation `hhalf : 2·c = 1` rather\nthan written as the field division `1/2`, so no `Field`/`field_simp` is\nneeded. Over a characteristic-zero field the unique such `c` is `1/2`, so\nthis specialises back to the previous statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.unit_eq_one_of_keystone_normalizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.unit_eq_one_of_keystone_normalizer","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/schwinger-measure-computational-time.lean#L78-L93","doc":"**Conditional unit forcing (proved, sorry-free).** GIVEN the\nidentification and the keystone-proved normalizer identity\n`(m+1) · N(m+1) = (m+1)!` — the `n·N(n) = n!` bridge of\n`QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding`, taken here as the named hypothesis\n`hkey` per the `_of_` discipline — the Schwinger measure unit is forced:\n`ς = 1`. The `m = 0` instance already decides it: `N 1 = 1! = 1` from the\nkeystone leg and `N 1 = ς · 0! = ς` from the identification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.BorelProperTimeIdentification.moment_eq_normalizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.BorelProperTimeIdentification.moment_eq_normalizer","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/schwinger-measure-computational-time.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The normalizer is the `ς`-unit proper-time moment: `N (m+1) = ς · m!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.BorelProperTimeIdentification.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.BorelProperTimeIdentification.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/schwinger-measure-computational-time.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.BorelProperTimeIdentification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchwingerMeasureComputationalTime.BorelProperTimeIdentification","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/schwinger-measure-computational-time.lean#L64-L76","doc":"**Primary conjecture (open — no instance).** The binding Borel variable\nis the loop proper time: the keystone-forced binding normalizer `N` is the\nmoment sequence of the Schwinger proper-time measure with unit `ς`. The\nquantitative content is the single field `moment_eq_normalizer`,\n`N (m + 1) = ς · m!` — the algebraic shadow of the integral representation\n`N(n) = ∫₀^∞ sⁿ e^{−s} ς ds/s = ς·(n−1)!` at `n = m + 1` (index shifted to\nkeep ℕ-subtraction out). An unproved primary conjecture is honestly\nrepresented by this content-bearing class with no instance. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:schwinger-measure-computational-time","label":"conj:schwinger-measure-computational-time","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/schwinger-measure-computational-time.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}